@* Compito 3, row 60: the list of the ACTIVE missions, as the WinForms FrmMISSIONS_LU showed them
   (FrmMISSIONS_LU.cs:51 reads them with GET /missions; :66 AddColumnsToGrid - every property of the
   mission, the Guid columns by device name except MissionId, GroupedMovementId and AssignmentGuid),
   and the one change that grid allowed: moving a mission onto another device (:92,
   SetMissionPositionAsync).
   <para>
   <b>Followed live.</b> Read once when the section is opened, then kept with the channel's
   MissionChanged on top (LiveMissionBoard: the events that arrive while a read is in flight are
   replayed on top of it), and read again whenever the feed says events may have gone by unseen
   (PlantLiveFeed.Resynced: the channel's opening, every reconnection, the host's resync signal).
   Shut, the list does nothing: an event or a resync only marks it stale, and it is read again when
   the section is opened.
   </para>
   <para>
   <b>Moving a mission is not an engine command.</b> PUT /missions/{id}/position answers at once -
   204, 404, 400 or 409 with the host's words (Wcs.Host MissionEndpoints), or 503 while the engine is
   still in Recover (MissionMoveProblems.EngineRecoveringTitle, owner's answer 4 of 8/10) or not loaded
   (ServiceUnavailableProblems.EngineNotLoaded in the problem's field, row 34 of the queue) - and has no
   command id and no CommandChanged to follow: the outcome IS the answer. It asks for no edit permit
   (MissionEndpoints maps it without RequiresEditPermission, and the WinForms grid moved missions
   while the engine ran) and it does not go through the page's write gate, which guards the plant's
   configuration. Confirmed in two steps on the page, like the engine switch. Never optimistic: the
   row moves when the host says so - the list is read again after a move that went through or whose
   outcome is unknown, and the channel's PositionChanged moves it too - and a refusal leaves the row
   as it was, with the host's own words on the outcome line (the Recover refusal with the page's own
   sentence).
   </para>
   <para>
   <b>Setting a mission's destination</b> (missions plan of 30/9, task 6) is the same kind of work:
   PUT /missions/{id}/destination, no edit permit, any engine state, the answer IS the outcome. The
   target picker serves both actions. The question names the load unit, the new destination and the
   one it replaces, and always shows the mission's gateway with the operator's choice on it (keep,
   clear or change it; none, or add one), keeping what there is preselected; the button that sends
   it is the one blue button. The engine computes the new route at once, also with the engine stopped, so the hover shows
   it on the canvas. Every refusal is said in plain words from the problem's TITLE (one per outcome,
   MissionDestinationProblems) and fields, never from the Italian detail; 400, 409, 422 and 503
   changed nothing the row shows that the channel would not say (a storage cell lost on the way is
   announced as a MissionChanged, and the refusal's lostTheCell field has the outcome line say it), so
   only a 204, a 404 and an answer that never came read the list again. After a 204 the gateway is
   said from the row read again, not from what was asked: the engine drops a gateway already reached. A route
   that the gateway blocks while one exists without it offers to send the same change again with the
   gateway cleared - if its row and its target are still the ones chosen when the refusal lands, and
   for as long as they stay chosen.
   </para>
   <para>
   <b>What the question says</b> (voce 39, task 7). Towards the warehouse it is already bound for, the
   question follows the gateway's radios: with the gateway as it is, a cell is asked again - another
   one when the row carries the operator's choice (OperatorDestination, row 44); with the
   gateway changed, the cell stays and only the route is computed again - promised only when the row
   has a cell. An extraction sent to a warehouse is told what happens to its order: picked up, the
   warehouse system already counts it as served; still in its cell, it becomes a change of cell, its
   order (when it has one) goes back free, and a refusal after the warehouse system was told closes
   the mission - the refusal does not say so, so that refusal too reads the list again, and the
   outcome says it when the row is gone. After an outcome that is not known, no other change of
   destination is asked until a read of the list that began after it goes through, and the outcome
   line ends with the row as the host has it then.
   </para>
   <para>
   <b>A change during a step</b> (item 54, decision 4 of the owner of 13/10). With a step of the mission
   in flight the host no longer refuses a move or a change of destination: it answers 202, and the
   change waits for the end of the step and is applied from where the step ends. The outcome line says
   "applied at the end of the movement", the list is read again, and the row carries the change that
   waits (MissionDto.PendingChange and PendingChangeItemId, two columns like every other) for as long as
   it waits - only in memory on the host (owner's answer 4 of 13/10), so its disappearance is seen. The
   chosen mission's line says it too.
   </para>
   <para>
   <b>A relocator and a precise cell</b> (item 54, decisions 5 and 6 of the owner of 13/10). Towards a
   relocator (a device a warehouse names as its relocator) the question asks "Deposit it, or only bring
   it there?", with nothing chosen, and the change is not sent until the operator answers; the choice
   travels in the body (MissionDestinationUpdate.AtTheRelocator) and the row shows it
   (MissionDto.RelocatorArrival). Towards a warehouse, or a relocator that is to deposit it, the cell is
   the warehouse system's to choose as before, or one the operator chooses: from the list the host asks
   the warehouse system for (GET /missions/{id}/storage-cells, the first 20 in the order of its search of
   every day, owner's answer 6), read once per question - an answer for a question no longer open is
   dropped - or written by its door A code in the field (answer 7). The precise cell goes alone in the
   body (CellDoorCode): through a relocator it is the relocator serving the cell that deposits it. Its
   refusals are said from the 422's field (cellRefusal), and the outcome names the cell in the warehouse
   the row read again carries.
   </para> *@
@using System.Globalization
@using System.Net
@using System.Text.Json
@using Wcs.Api.Client
@using Wcs.Api.Contracts
@using Wcs.Api.Contracts.Dtos
@using Wcs.WebEditor.Drawio.Coordination
@using Wcs.WebEditor.Live
@using Wcs.WebEditor.Model
@using Wcs.WebEditor.Session
@using static Wcs.Common.Enums
@inherits DrawioListSection
@implements IDisposable
@inject EditorSessionState Session

<button type="button" id="drawio-mission-list-toggle" class="drawio-section-toggle" aria-label="Missions"
        aria-pressed="@(Open ? "true" : "false")" @onclick="ToggleAsync">
    <DrawioIcon Name="missions" />
    <span class="drawio-toggle-label">Missions</span>
</button>
@{
    // Once per render, before the window: its title bar counts the rows the list shows.
    var rows = Open ? VisibleRows().ToList() : null;
}
<DrawioWindow Id="drawio-mission-list" Class="drawio-mission-list" Title="Missions" Icon="missions"
              Count="@(!_board.HasRead || rows is null ? null : rows.Count.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture))"
              Help="@(Open ? ScopeNote : null)" Open="Open" OnClose="CloseAsync" Place="Place">
    @if (rows is not null)
    {
        var pageCount = PageCount(rows.Count);
        var currentPage = Math.Min(_page, pageCount);
        var pageRows = rows.Skip((currentPage - 1) * PageSize).Take(PageSize).ToList();
        var displayColumns = DisplayColumns();
        <div class="drawio-mission-list-body">
            <div class="drawio-device-list-tools">
                <span class="drawio-filter">
                    <DrawioIcon Name="search" />
                    <input type="search" id="drawio-mission-list-filter" class="drawio-device-list-filter"
                           aria-label="Filter missions"
                           placeholder="Filter on any field: LU, source, destination, status..." value="@Filter" @oninput="FilterMissionsTyped" />
                </span>
                <div class="drawio-mission-view-switch" role="group" aria-label="Mission table view">
                    <button type="button" id="drawio-mission-list-view-compact"
                            class="@(!_extended ? "drawio-mission-view-active" : null)"
                            aria-pressed="@(!_extended ? "true" : "false")" @onclick="() => SetExtended(false)">Compact</button>
                    <button type="button" id="drawio-mission-list-view-extended"
                            class="@(_extended ? "drawio-mission-view-active" : null)"
                            aria-pressed="@(_extended ? "true" : "false")" @onclick="() => SetExtended(true)">Extended</button>
                </div>
                <span class="drawio-mission-field-count">@(_extended ? $"{Columns.Count}/{Columns.Count} current fields" : $"{CompactColumnKeys.Count} operational fields")</span>
                <span id="drawio-mission-list-count" class="drawio-device-list-count">@CountLine(rows.Count)</span>
                <button type="button" id="drawio-mission-list-reread" disabled="@_board.Reading" @onclick="ReadAsync">Read again</button>
            </div>
            @if (_board.Reading)
            {
                <p id="drawio-mission-list-reading" class="drawio-operations-outcome">Reading the missions from the host...</p>
            }
            @if (_readError is { } readError)
            {
                <DrawioFailureLine Id="drawio-mission-list-read-error" Class="drawio-operations-error" Text="@readError.Text" Detail="@readError.Detail" />
            }
            <section id="drawio-mission-move" class="drawio-mission-move">
                @if (_chosen is { } chosenId)
                {
                    var chosen = _board.Find(chosenId);
                    <p id="drawio-mission-move-chosen" class="drawio-mission-selection-summary">
                        @if (chosen is null)
                        {
                            @($"The mission {chosenId} is no longer active on the host: there is nothing to move or to send elsewhere.")
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            @($"Chosen: {MissionName(chosen)}, now on {DeviceName(chosen.PositionItemId)}, {BoundFor(chosen.DestinationItemId)}.{WaitingLine(chosen)}")
                        }
                    </p>
                    <div class="drawio-test-route-endpoints">
                        <input type="search" id="drawio-mission-move-search" placeholder="Search a device by name"
                               disabled="@Asking" value="@_targetSearch"
                               @oninput="e => _targetSearch = e.Value as string ?? string.Empty" />
                        <select id="drawio-mission-move-target" disabled="@Asking"
                                value="@(_target?.ToString() ?? string.Empty)" @onchange="TargetPicked">
                            <option value="">(choose a device)</option>
                            @foreach (var device in Candidates(_targetSearch, _target))
                            {
                                <option value="@device.ItemId">@NameOf(device)</option>
                            }
                        </select>
                        <button type="button" id="drawio-mission-move-use-selected"
                                disabled="@(SelectedItemId is null || Asking)"
                                @onclick="UseSelected">Use selected on the drawing</button>
                    </div>
                    <p id="drawio-mission-move-selected" class="drawio-test-route-selected">
                        Selected on the drawing: @(SelectedItemId is null ? "(nothing selected)" : SelectedItemName)
                    </p>
                    <span id="drawio-mission-move-target-chosen">Target: @(_target is { } target ? DeviceName(target) : "(none chosen)")</span>
                    @if (_pending is { } pending)
                    {
                        <div>
                            <span id="drawio-mission-move-question" class="drawio-operations-question">Move @pending.Mission from @pending.From to @pending.Target?</span>
                            <button type="button" id="drawio-mission-move-confirm" @onclick="ConfirmMoveAsync">Yes</button>
                            <button type="button" id="drawio-mission-move-cancel" @onclick="() => _pending = null">Cancel</button>
                        </div>
                    }
                    else if (_pendingDestination is { } asked)
                    {
                        <div id="drawio-mission-destination-box" class="drawio-mission-destination-box">
                            <span id="drawio-mission-destination-question" class="drawio-operations-question">@QuestionOf(asked)</span>
                            @* The mission's gateway, always shown, with what there is kept unless the operator says otherwise. *@
                            <fieldset id="drawio-mission-destination-gateway" class="drawio-mission-destination-gateway">
                                <legend id="drawio-mission-destination-gateway-now">Gateway: @(asked.GatewayName ?? "none")</legend>
                                @if (asked.GatewayName is not null)
                                {
                                    @GatewayOption("keep", "Keep it", GatewayChoice.Keep)
                                    @GatewayOption("clear", "Clear it", GatewayChoice.Clear)
                                    @GatewayOption("change", "Change it", GatewayChoice.Change)
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    @GatewayOption("none", "None", GatewayChoice.Keep)
                                    @GatewayOption("add", "Add one", GatewayChoice.Change)
                                }
                                @if (_gatewayChoice == GatewayChoice.Change)
                                {
                                    <div class="drawio-test-route-endpoints">
                                        <input type="search" id="drawio-mission-destination-gateway-search" placeholder="Search a device by name"
                                               value="@_gatewaySearch" @oninput="e => _gatewaySearch = e.Value as string ?? string.Empty" />
                                        <select id="drawio-mission-destination-gateway-target"
                                                value="@(_gateway?.ToString() ?? string.Empty)" @onchange="GatewayPicked">
                                            <option value="">(choose a device)</option>
                                            @foreach (var device in Candidates(_gatewaySearch, _gateway))
                                            {
                                                <option value="@device.ItemId">@NameOf(device)</option>
                                            }
                                        </select>
                                    </div>
                                }
                            </fieldset>
                            @* Item 54, decision 5: towards a relocator the operator says what it does with the load unit. *@
                            @if (asked.TargetIsRelocator)
                            {
                                <fieldset id="drawio-mission-destination-relocator" class="drawio-mission-destination-gateway">
                                    <legend id="drawio-mission-destination-relocator-question">Deposit it, or only bring it there?</legend>
                                    @ArrivalOption("deposit", "Deposit it", MissionRelocatorArrival.Deposit)
                                    @ArrivalOption("stay", "Only bring it there", MissionRelocatorArrival.Stay)
                                </fieldset>
                            }
                            @* Item 54, decision 6: the cell, chosen by the warehouse system as always, or by the operator. *@
                            @if (CellCanBeChosen(asked))
                            {
                                <fieldset id="drawio-mission-destination-cell" class="drawio-mission-destination-gateway">
                                    <legend>Storage cell</legend>
                                    @CellOption("warehouse", "Chosen by the warehouse system", CellChoice.ByTheWarehouse)
                                    @CellOption("precise", "A cell I choose", CellChoice.Precise)
                                    @if (_cellChoice == CellChoice.Precise)
                                    {
                                        <div class="drawio-mission-destination-cell-pick">
                                            @if (_cellList is { Loading: true })
                                            {
                                                <span id="drawio-mission-destination-cell-reading" class="drawio-operations-outcome">Asking the warehouse system for the cells...</span>
                                            }
                                            else if (_cellList is { Failure: { } listFailure })
                                            {
                                                <DrawioFailureLine Id="drawio-mission-destination-cell-error" Class="drawio-operations-error"
                                                                   Text="@listFailure.Text" Detail="@listFailure.Detail" />
                                            }
                                            else if (_cellList is { Cells: { } cells })
                                            {
                                                <span id="drawio-mission-destination-cell-listed" class="drawio-operations-outcome">@CellsLine(asked, cells.Count)</span>
                                                @if (cells.Count > 0)
                                                {
                                                    <select id="drawio-mission-destination-cell-list" value="@(cells.Any(c => c.DoorCode == _cellCode.Trim()) ? _cellCode.Trim() : string.Empty)"
                                                            @onchange="e => _cellCode = e.Value as string ?? string.Empty">
                                                        <option value="">(choose a cell)</option>
                                                        @foreach (var cell in cells)
                                                        {
                                                            <option value="@cell.DoorCode">@CellName(cell)</option>
                                                        }
                                                    </select>
                                                }
                                            }
                                            <label class="drawio-mission-destination-option">
                                                Door A code of the cell
                                                <input type="text" id="drawio-mission-destination-cell-code" placeholder="for example 3B02.0363.0001"
                                                       value="@_cellCode" @oninput="e => _cellCode = e.Value as string ?? string.Empty" />
                                            </label>
                                        </div>
                                    }
                                </fieldset>
                            }
                            <div class="drawio-mission-actions">
                                <button type="button" id="drawio-mission-destination-confirm" class="drawio-btn-primary"
                                        disabled="@(!CanConfirmDestination(asked))"
                                        @onclick="ConfirmDestinationAsync">Set destination</button>
                                <button type="button" id="drawio-mission-destination-cancel" @onclick="() => _pendingDestination = null">Cancel</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="drawio-mission-actions">
                            <button type="button" id="drawio-mission-move-button" class="drawio-mission-action-position"
                                    disabled="@(!CanMove(chosen))" @onclick="() => AskToMove(chosen)">Change position</button>
                            <button type="button" id="drawio-mission-destination-button" class="drawio-mission-action-destination"
                                    disabled="@(!CanSetDestination(chosen))" @onclick="() => AskToSetDestination(chosen)">Send elsewhere</button>
                        </div>
                    }
                }
                else
                {
                    <p id="drawio-mission-move-hint" class="drawio-operations-outcome">Click a mission's row to move it onto another device or to set its destination.</p>
                }
                @if (_sending is { } sending)
                {
                    <p id="drawio-mission-move-sending" class="drawio-operations-outcome">@sending</p>
                }
                @* One outcome line for the section: the last of the two actions. *@
                @if (_outcome is { } moveOutcome)
                {
                    <DrawioFailureLine Id="drawio-mission-move-outcome" LineClass="drawio-operations-outcome"
                                       Class="@(_went ? "drawio-device-list-written" : "drawio-device-list-not-written")"
                                       Text="@moveOutcome.Text" Detail="@moveOutcome.Detail" />
                }
                @if (_withoutTheGateway is not null && !Asking)
                {
                    <button type="button" id="drawio-mission-destination-clear-gateway" class="drawio-btn-primary"
                            @onclick="ClearTheGatewayAndSetAsync">Clear the gateway and set destination</button>
                }
            </section>
            @if (GoToOutcome is { } goTo)
            {
                <DrawioFailureLine Id="drawio-mission-list-goto" LineClass="drawio-operations-outcome" Text="@goTo.Text" Detail="@goTo.Detail" />
            }
            @if (_board.HasRead)
            {
                <section id="drawio-mission-list-grid" class="drawio-mission-grid">
                    <div class="drawio-list-scroll drawio-mission-grid-scroll">
                        <table id="drawio-mission-list-table" class="drawio-list-table drawio-mission-table @(_extended ? "drawio-mission-table-extended" : "drawio-mission-table-compact")">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    @foreach (var column in displayColumns)
                                    {
                                        <th data-column="@column.Key" hidden="@ColumnHidden(column.Key)"
                                            class="@HeaderClass(column.Key)" aria-sort="@AriaSort(column.Key)"
                                            @onclick="() => SortMissionsBy(column.Key)">@column.Label</th>
                                    }
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                @foreach (var mission in pageRows)
                                {
                                    var selected = mission.MissionId == _chosen;
                                    <tr data-mission-id="@mission.MissionId" aria-selected="@(selected ? "true" : "false")"
                                        class="@(selected ? "drawio-list-row drawio-list-row-selected" : "drawio-list-row")"
                                        @onclick="() => ChooseAsync(mission)">
                                        @foreach (var column in displayColumns)
                                        {
                                            <td data-column="@column.Key" hidden="@ColumnHidden(column.Key)"
                                                class="@CellClass(column.Key, mission)">@column.TextOf(mission, DeviceName)</td>
                                        }
                                    </tr>
                                }
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <footer class="drawio-mission-pager" aria-label="Mission pages">
                        <span id="drawio-mission-list-page-summary" aria-live="polite">@PageLine(rows.Count, currentPage)</span>
                        <div class="drawio-mission-page-buttons">
                            <button type="button" id="drawio-mission-list-previous" aria-label="Previous page"
                                    disabled="@(currentPage == 1)" @onclick="() => GoToPage(currentPage - 1, pageCount)">‹</button>
                            @foreach (var pageNumber in PageChoices(currentPage, pageCount))
                            {
                                <button type="button" class="@(pageNumber == currentPage ? "drawio-mission-page-active" : null)"
                                        aria-label="Page @pageNumber" aria-current="@(pageNumber == currentPage ? "page" : null)"
                                        @onclick="() => GoToPage(pageNumber, pageCount)">@pageNumber</button>
                            }
                            <button type="button" id="drawio-mission-list-next" aria-label="Next page"
                                    disabled="@(currentPage == pageCount)" @onclick="() => GoToPage(currentPage + 1, pageCount)">›</button>
                        </div>
                    </footer>
                </section>
            }
        </div>
    }
</DrawioWindow>

@code {
    /// <summary>What the list is: the paragraph that opened the window until the passata grafica, word for word, behind the "?" of its title bar while the window is open.</summary>
    private static readonly RenderFragment ScopeNote =
        @<p class="drawio-mission-list-scope">
            Every active mission, as the host has it, followed live. Click a row to select on the drawing the
            device the mission is on, and to choose that mission to move it onto another device or to set its
            destination.
        </p>;

    /// <summary>The plant as the page holds it: the devices' names, and the targets a mission can be moved onto.</summary>
    [Parameter] public PlantGraph? Graph { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public PlantLiveFeed? Feed { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The device selected on the drawing (DrawioSelectionState.ConfigItemId): what "Use selected on the drawing" takes as the target.</summary>
    [Parameter] public Guid? SelectedItemId { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? SelectedItemName { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What the drawing answered to the last row chosen here, worded by the page; what its script threw, if it did not answer, is behind the line's "?".</summary>
    [Parameter] public DrawioSaid? GoToOutcome { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A row was chosen: the page selects on the drawing the device the mission is on.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<MissionDto> OnSelect { get; set; }

    /// <summary>FrmMISSIONS_LU.cs:66: every property of the mission; the Guid columns are devices, except these three.</summary>
    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<DrawioDtoColumn<MissionDto>> Columns =
        DrawioDtoColumn<MissionDto>.Of(nameof(MissionDto.MissionId), nameof(MissionDto.GroupedMovementId), nameof(MissionDto.AssignmentGuid));

    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<string> ColumnKeys = [.. Columns.Select(column => column.Key)];
    private static readonly Dictionary<string, DrawioDtoColumn<MissionDto>> ColumnByKey = Columns.ToDictionary(column => column.Key);

    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<string> CompactColumnKeys =
    [
        nameof(MissionDto.LoadUnitId), nameof(MissionDto.LoadUnitCode), nameof(MissionDto.PositionItemId),
        nameof(MissionDto.SourceItemId), nameof(MissionDto.DestinationItemId), nameof(MissionDto.Status),
        nameof(MissionDto.StorageDoorCode), nameof(MissionDto.PickUpDoorCode), nameof(MissionDto.MissionType),
        nameof(MissionDto.OperationType),
    ];

    private static readonly HashSet<string> CompactColumnKeySet = [.. CompactColumnKeys];
    private const int PageSize = 10;
    private bool _extended;
    private int _page = 1;

    /// <summary>A move asked and not confirmed yet: what the question names, frozen when "Move" was pressed.</summary>
    private sealed record PendingMove(Guid MissionId, Guid TargetId, string Mission, string From, string Target);

    /// <summary>
    /// A change of destination asked and not confirmed yet, frozen when "Set destination" was pressed:
    /// the load unit as the operator knows it (and how a sentence starts with it), where it is (its
    /// identifier, null: nowhere, and its name), the new destination, the one it replaces (null: none)
    /// and the mission's gateway (null: none) - the words of the question and of the outcome. The
    /// target is a warehouse also when it is a group of warehouses: the engine reserves a cell in one
    /// of them. <see cref="Again"/>: the destination it
    /// has, or the group of the warehouse it has (the engine writes the member it reserved in);
    /// <see cref="HasCell"/>: the row has a storage door; <see cref="OperatorChose"/>: the row carries the
    /// mark of the operator's choice (<see cref="MissionDto.OperatorDestination"/>); <see cref="Order"/>: what the change does to
    /// the order of an extraction sent to a warehouse (null: nothing); <see cref="ChangeOfCell"/>: an
    /// extraction still in its cell sent to a warehouse its position does not reach, which the engine
    /// turns into a change of cell. Item 54: <see cref="TargetIsRelocator"/>: a warehouse names the target
    /// as its relocator (decision 5, MissionGateway.IsARelocator); <see cref="CellOrder"/> and
    /// <see cref="CellChangeOfCell"/>: the same as <see cref="Order"/> and <see cref="ChangeOfCell"/> for a
    /// precise cell chosen through a relocator, which the engine treats as a change towards the
    /// warehouse of the cell (decision 6).
    /// </summary>
    private sealed record PendingDestination(Guid MissionId, Guid TargetId, string LoadUnit, string LoadUnitFirst, Guid? PositionId, string Position,
        string Target, bool TargetIsStorage, Guid? CurrentId, string? Current, Guid? GatewayId, string? GatewayName,
        bool Again, bool HasCell, bool OperatorChose, string? Order, bool ChangeOfCell,
        bool TargetIsRelocator = false, string? CellOrder = null, bool CellChangeOfCell = false)
    {
        /// <summary>
        /// The question, with the gateway as the radios leave it (<paramref name="through"/>: null when
        /// they do not change it, otherwise how the new gateway is said). The same warehouse again
        /// (decisions 5 and 6 of 2/10, MissionGateway.ChangeToStorageAsync): with the gateway as it is,
        /// a request for a cell there again - another one when the operator had chosen it (the engine
        /// leaves out the cell it has, MissionGateway.CellToReplaceAsync), possibly the same one when the
        /// engine had. The row says which (<see cref="OperatorChose"/>; row 44 of the queue, owner's
        /// decision of 10/10), and the question says only that one. With the gateway
        /// changed the mission keeps the cell it has and only its route is computed again - with or
        /// without the operator's choice. Without a cell on the row there is nothing to keep: the
        /// request asks for one whatever the gateway, and the question promises nothing.
        /// </summary>
        public string QuestionWith(string? through)
        {
            var question = Current is null ? $"Send {LoadUnit} to {Target}?"
                : !Again ? $"Send {LoadUnit} to {Target} instead of {Current}?"
                : !TargetIsStorage ? $"Send {LoadUnit} to {Target} again?"
                : !HasCell ? $"Send {LoadUnit} to {Target} again? It has no cell there now: this asks the warehouse system for one in {Target}."
                : through is not null ? $"Send {LoadUnit} to {Target} again{through}? It keeps the cell it has in {Target}: only its route is computed again."
                : (OperatorChose
                      ? $"Send {LoadUnit} to {Target} again? This asks the warehouse system for another cell in {Target}."
                      : $"Send {LoadUnit} to {Target} again? This asks the warehouse system for a cell in {Target} again.")
                  + " Changing the gateway instead keeps the cell it has and only computes its route again.";
            return Order is null ? question : $"{question} {Order}";
        }

        /// <summary>
        /// The question with a precise cell (item 54, decision 6): the cell by its code, in the target -
        /// a warehouse, a group of warehouses, or the relocator that deposits it - and what the warehouse
        /// system does with it. No cell is kept: the operator chose one.
        /// </summary>
        public string QuestionWithTheCell(string code, string? through)
        {
            var into = TargetIsRelocator ? $"into the cell {code}, deposited by {Target}" : $"into the cell {code} of {Target}";
            var instead = Current is null || Again ? "" : $" instead of {Current}";
            var question = $"Send {LoadUnit} {into}{through}{instead}? The warehouse system checks that the cell is free and suits it, "
                           + "and reserves it; otherwise the change is refused with the reason.";
            var order = TargetIsRelocator ? CellOrder : Order;
            return order is null ? question : $"{question} {order}";
        }

        /// <summary>Where the load unit still goes after a refusal: nothing changed.</summary>
        public string Still => Current is null ? "It still has no destination." : $"It is still bound for {Current}.";
    }

    /// <summary>Where the cell comes from (item 54, decision 6): the warehouse system chooses it, as always, or the operator.</summary>
    private enum CellChoice { ByTheWarehouse, Precise }

    /// <summary>
    /// The cells the warehouse system proposes for the question open now (GET /missions/{id}/storage-cells):
    /// on their way, read (<see cref="Cells"/>, the first 20 in the order of its search of every day), or
    /// not read (<see cref="Failure"/>). Kept with the mission and the target it was asked for, so that an
    /// answer for a question no longer open is not shown under another.
    /// </summary>
    private sealed record CellList(Guid MissionId, Guid TargetId, bool Loading, List<StorageCellCandidateDto>? Cells, DrawioSaid? Failure);

    /// <summary>What the operator chose for the gateway: keep what there is (also nothing), clear it, or set the device picked.</summary>
    private enum GatewayChoice { Keep, Clear, Change }

    /// <summary>
    /// A change of destination as it goes to the host: the question it answers, the choice on the gateway,
    /// and the name of the device to set (only with Set); item 54, what the relocator does with the load
    /// unit (decision 5) or the precise cell's door A code (decision 6), never both.
    /// </summary>
    private sealed record DestinationRequest(PendingDestination Asked, MissionGatewayUpdate Gateway, string? NewGatewayName,
        MissionRelocatorArrival? Arrival = null, string? CellCode = null)
    {
        /// <summary>The change of cell the request makes of an extraction still in its cell: through a relocator only a precise cell makes one.</summary>
        public bool ChangeOfCell => Asked.TargetIsRelocator ? CellCode is not null && Asked.CellChangeOfCell : Asked.ChangeOfCell;
    }

    /// <summary>A change of destination whose outcome is not known, and the outcome line that said so: the next request waits for a read of the list that started after it.</summary>
    private sealed record NotKnown(PendingDestination Asked, DrawioSaid Outcome);

    private readonly LiveMissionBoard _board = new();
    private DrawioSaid? _readError;

    /// <summary>A reason to read again arrived while a read was in flight: exactly one more read follows it.</summary>
    private bool _readAgain;

    /// <summary>Something may have changed while the section was shut: it is read again when it is opened.</summary>
    private bool _stale;

    private bool _wasOpen;
    private PlantLiveFeed? _subscribedFeed;
    private bool _disposed;

    private Guid? _chosen;
    private Guid? _target;
    private string _targetSearch = "";
    private PendingMove? _pending;
    private PendingDestination? _pendingDestination;
    private GatewayChoice _gatewayChoice;
    private Guid? _gateway;
    private string _gatewaySearch = "";

    /// <summary>Item 54, decision 5: what the relocator does with the load unit, as the operator chose it; null until chosen.</summary>
    private MissionRelocatorArrival? _arrival;

    /// <summary>Item 54, decision 6: where the cell comes from, and the code of the one the operator chose (from the list, or written).</summary>
    private CellChoice _cellChoice;
    private string _cellCode = "";
    private CellList? _cellList;

    /// <summary>What the section is asking the host now, said on the page; null when nothing is on its way. One request at a time.</summary>
    private string? _sending;

    /// <summary>
    /// The outcome of the last of the two actions: one sentence, and what the host answered - or the
    /// failure's own type and message - behind its "?" (row 37 of the queue, extended to the whole page
    /// on 10/10), where the host's words used to be quoted in it.
    /// </summary>
    private DrawioSaid? _outcome;
    private bool _went;

    /// <summary>
    /// The change whose outcome is not known (d6 §8, the retry trap): until a read of the list that
    /// began after it goes through, no other change of destination is asked. A gateway-only change
    /// that went through, sent again from the row as it was, would find the gateway already written and
    /// ask the warehouse system for another cell; read again, the row and the question show the gateway
    /// as the host has it now.
    /// </summary>
    private NotKnown? _readBeforeAsking;

    /// <summary>The change the gateway blocked while there is a route without it: the same change, ready to go again with the gateway cleared - while its row and its target are the ones chosen.</summary>
    private DestinationRequest? _withoutTheGateway;

    /// <summary>A question is open or a request is on its way: the target cannot change under it.</summary>
    private bool Asking => _pending is not null || _pendingDestination is not null || _sending is not null;

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (!ReferenceEquals(Feed, _subscribedFeed))
        {
            if (_subscribedFeed is not null)
            {
                _subscribedFeed.MissionChanged -= OnMissionChanged;
                _subscribedFeed.Resynced -= OnResynced;
            }

            _subscribedFeed = Feed;
            if (Feed is not null)
            {
                Feed.MissionChanged += OnMissionChanged;
                Feed.Resynced += OnResynced;
            }
        }

        var opened = Open && !_wasOpen;
        _wasOpen = Open;
        var readNow = opened && (!_board.HasRead || _stale) && !_board.Reading;
        if (readNow) _ = ReadAsync();
        // Opened again while a read started before the shutting is still on its way, and something
        // happened while shut (an event, a resync): that answer may predate it, so exactly one more
        // read follows it. Without this the list stayed wrong while open (fix round 1).
        else if (opened && _stale && _board.Reading) _readAgain = true;

        ParametersArrived((Graph, Graph?.Revision, SelectedItemId, SelectedItemName, GoToOutcome), renderAnyway: readNow);
    }

    private string CountLine(int visible) => !_board.HasRead
        ? "Not read yet."
        : string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Filter)
            ? $"{_board.Rows.Count} active missions."
            : $"{visible} of {_board.Rows.Count} active missions.";

